# Heat leaving through the top surface. For any realistic air flow it is negligible next to conduction to the substrate.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Standard shifter with a liquid-cooled or heat-sunk top above (h = 100000 W/m2K)
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=60 ymin=-10 ymax=5
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 5
rect si -0.25 0.25 2 2.25
rect tin -1 1 4 4.25
heater h xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=4 ymax=4.25 power=0.1
probe wg xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=2 ymax=2.25
top convective h=100000
expect response wg h 145.643319 1e-7
expect pi_power wg h 28.6087044 1e-7
expect peak 36.0301446 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 14400
